index 000000000..e27a6e843
--- /dev/null
+++ b/releasenotes/notes/deployer-checks-5c3bf4aaabef98ac.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+features:
+  - |
+    Kolla Ansible now records what last changed each host in
+    ``/etc/kolla/kolla-ansible-deployment.json``, after each successful
+    ``deploy``, ``deploy-containers``, ``reconfigure``, ``upgrade`` and
+    ``migrate-container-engine``. The record holds the release, the Kolla
+    Ansible version and git commit, the images' tag, the action and the time.
+    It is written whatever ``--tags`` were given, because a partial deploy has
+    still changed the host.
+  - |
+    When Kolla Ansible runs from a containerised deployer image, every action
+    except ``destroy`` first checks the deployer. It refuses an
+    ``openstack_tag`` or ``openstack_release`` that differs from the image's.
+    It refuses a host whose record shows an older release, or the same
+    release with an older Kolla Ansible version. Before an upgrade, a deployer
+    for a newer release may run only ``bootstrap-servers``, ``pull``,
+    ``prechecks``, ``gather-facts`` and ``upgrade``, and ``upgrade`` may move
+    only to the next release, or from a ``.1`` release to the next ``.1``.
+    ``master`` counts as newer than every release, so a host last deployed
+    from ``master`` refuses a deployer for a stable release. The new
+    ``--override-deployer-checks`` option turns each refusal into a warning.
+    Kolla Ansible installed with ``pip`` writes the record but does not check
+    it.
